Topic cuts: {{none | one line each:}}
- {{TOPIC}}: not on {{EXAM}} ({{SOURCE: Ed #N, a staff post, date | the syllabus, its line}});
  {{WHAT STAYS, if part of it does}}.

- **Scope:** `in`; `in, PDF pp.A-B` (with the last in-scope slide as "PDF p.N = printed M"), or
  `in, PDF pp.A-B, C-D` for two ranges; `in, slides #/A-#/B` for a reveal deck (horizontal slide
  indexes); `concepts only`; `reserved: <exam>`, copied raw and never rendered, extracted or
  opened; `pending: <planned scope>`, not here yet, its scope fixed at intake and written in one
  of the `in` forms when the file arrives; `out`. Notes go in parentheses, and never hold a page
  range (it would go unchecked); `extract_check.py` refuses any other wording.
- **By:** who made the source, which the page's source key shows: `staff` (the course's own
  slides, sets and posts), `classmate` (a shared study guide), `textbook`, `student` (the student's
  own notes), or a few words of free text. Optional: a table without the column still reads, and
  its key then has no Made by column.
- **Notes:** `<what it is>[; <remark>]`, free text that no script parses for answers. What the
  source is, in a few words ("Lecture 4: search"), is what the source key shows, the file name
  under it; with it empty the key shows the file name alone. A remark on the row (why a range is
  cut, when a file arrives) follows a `;` and stays off the page, so what it is holds no `;` of
  its own.
- **Answers:** `yes` marks a file that holds answers (official solutions, a past exam's key).
  - Only an in-scope row (`in` or `concepts only`) answers anything. Its answers are extracted into
    `_build/solutions/`, one file per set, `_build/solutions/<name>.md` beside each set's extract
    `_build/extract/<name>.md` (each part's solution under its part; a separate answers file's
    pages, or a past exam's key pages or sections), never into an extract. An answers file that
    solves several sets keeps its own pages in `_build/solutions/<answers file name>.md`, each
    holding only the line `(transcribed under the sets' blocks)`: its text sits in each set's own
    file. A past exam's other pages (the cover, the rules, a formula sheet) stay in its extract
    (`02-extract`). Mock writers never read `_build/solutions/`.
  - Nothing published quotes a set's official solution until the student has attempted every part
    of that set, which the set's own row then records in its Answers cell: `no, attempted
    YYYY-MM-DD` for a set with no key of its own (`HW1` above), `yes, attempted YYYY-MM-DD` for a
    doc holding its own key (a past exam). A separate answers file's row (Key `for ...`) stays
    `yes` and never records an attempt, since it may solve several sets. Until the
    set's own row says `attempted`, `05-verify` step 5's questions check treats it as
    unattempted.
- **Key:** what an Answers `yes` row answers and where its answers sit. `01-ingest` writes it after
  looking at the file, in exactly one of these forms, and `extract_check.py` reads the whole cell:
  - empty or `-`: not an answers doc (and a `pending` row until its file arrives);
  - `for HW1, HW2 and HW3`: a separate answers file, naming the sets it solves, each a doc id of
    this table (`KEY NAMES NO DOC` otherwise) and never its own row's (`KEY NAMES ITS OWN DOC`: a
    doc holding its own key takes one of the forms below);
  - `pp. 7-9, 11` or `p.N`: a doc holding its own key (a past exam), on those pages, only for a
    PDF, whatever Pages holds (`PAGES KEY ON AN UNPAGED DOC` otherwise);
  - `inline`: a doc holding its own key, each solution under its question on the same page, so
    no page is a key page;
  - `sections: Marking scheme, Answers`: a source without pages, a Word file or a slide deck,
    whose key is the sections or slides with exactly those locators (`### [PE3 Marking scheme]
    ...`; a deck's slides as `sections: #/5, #/6`); a block whose locator is such a name
    followed by ` Q...` or a comma is key material too. A paged doc fails it (`SECTIONS KEY ON A
    PAGED DOC`).
  - `extract_check.py` fails an in-scope Answers `yes` row with an empty Key cell (`NO KEY`),
    any other wording (`UNREAD KEY`), and a filled Key cell on a row whose Answers isn't `yes`
    (`KEY WITHOUT ANSWERS`). A row on a STATUS `Unverified:` line solves nothing until verified.
- **Topic cuts** name what the exam leaves out inside an `in` range, which no page range can say
  ("negative weights are not on Exam 1", from a staff post). They are a list under the table, never
  a second table, and scope like the rows: `03-backbone` marks the subsections a cut reaches and
  what of them stays, the notes keep the material it takes out under a `Not on <exam>` banner
  (`04-write`), and the sheets, mocks and cram order leave that material out (a mock written before
  a later cut keeps it, and the cram order's line for that mock says to skip it: `10-polish`).
- **The exam-details file** (a syllabus, an announcement) is `in`: its facts go to CLAUDE.md, and
  `03-backbone` maps its blocks `skip`.
- **Pages** come from `pdfinfo`, which reads a file's metadata, not its pages: a `reserved` row
  gets its count that way and stays unopened.
- **Doc ids** are what citations use (`[D4 p.17]`): keep them short, and never renumber one.
